{{also|Goose}}
==English==
{{wikipedia|goose (disambiguation)|goose|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|ǵʰh₂éns}}
From {{inh|en|enm|goos}}, {{m|enm|gos}}, from {{inh|en|ang|gōs}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*gans}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*gans}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*ǵʰh₂éns}}.

{{rel-top|Cognates:}}
Compare {{cog|fy|goes}}, {{cog|frr|göis}} (also Fering-Öömrang dialect {{cog|frr|gus}}; Sölring dialect {{cog|frr|Guus}}; Heligoland dialect {{cog|frr|gus}}), {{cog|nds|Goos}}, {{cog|nds|Gans}}, {{cog|nl|gans}}, {{cog|de|Gans}}, {{cog|da|-}}, {{cog|sv|-}} and {{cog|no|gås}}, {{cog|is|gæs}}, {{cog|ga|gé}}, {{cog|la|ānser}}, {{cog|lv|zoss|zùoss}}, {{cog|ru|гусь}}, {{cog|sq|gatë}}, {{cog|grc|χήν}}, {{cog|ae|𐬰𐬁}}, {{cog|sa|हंस|tr=haṃsá}}. {{rel-bottom}}

* The [[tailor's iron]] is so called from the likeness of the handle to the neck of a goose.
* The verb sense of pinching the buttocks is derived from a goose's inclination to bite at a retreating intruder's hindquarters.

